From 2610051adbd18719d04e0282e69f87bb4638eb32 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Andr=C3=A9=20Machado?= <machaddr@falanet.org>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 15:53:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] drm/bridge: cdns-dsi: deassert JH7110 RXESC reset
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The StarFive vendor display driver deasserts the Cadence DSI RXESC
reset before sending panel commands. Leaving it asserted can prevent the
receive side used for command acknowledgements from operating.

Add RXESC to the wrapper reset bulk. Order the array so the reset
framework deasserts SYS, TXESC, RXESC and DPI, matching the vendor
sequence. Keep TXBYTEHS last and asserted until the D-PHY high-speed
path is ready.

Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/cadence/cdns-dsi-jh7110.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/cadence/cdns-dsi-jh7110.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/cadence/cdns-dsi-jh7110.c
index cc97f9ecc6820..86a9450adeacd 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/cadence/cdns-dsi-jh7110.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/cadence/cdns-dsi-jh7110.c
@@ -19,9 +19,10 @@
 #define JH7110_VOUT_SYSCON_LCD_TO_DSI	BIT(3)
 
 static const char * const dsi_resets[] = {
-	"sys",
 	"dpi",
+	"rxesc",
 	"txesc",
+	"sys",
 	"txbytehs",
 };
 
